    "excerpt":"Longer write-ups of projects, with interactive figures.           Final project · Computational Statistical Physics · ETH Zürich · 2026     Simulating the 3D Heisenberg magnet     Ising and Heisenberg spins, Metropolis and Wolff updates, and finite-size scaling, with live simulations and the measured Tc and critical exponents.           Semester project · Atmospheric Physics, ETH Zürich · 2026     How strong can a hurricane get?     Potential intensity from the Carnot cycle, when the bound fails, the ERA5 reanalysis, and what regridding and time-averaging do to the inputs.           Methods comparison · tools from summer research, University of Edinburgh · 2025     JAX-CFD and Dedalus on Kolmogorov flow     Two spectral solvers on the same 2D flow: an exact solution, the onset of instability, chaos at Re = 40, turbulence at Re = 2000, cost and gradients, with a live solver.           Summer research · University of Edinburgh · 2024     The three-body problem     Three centuries of history, symplectic integrators and energy drift, a map of periodic orbits with a live 3D view, and the figure-eight proof.      For research publications and the three-body problem project, see Research.  ","url": "https://henry-yip.github.io/projects/"
